                        $tmp_data_TEXT = 'This is a solution to add support
for a use case where the CRNRSTN ::
Lightsaber RoCEv2 SOAP Services Layer 
(CLR-SSL) is managing response return 
and handling multiple CRNRSTN :: Lightsaber
mapped return types within a single
mapped response.

I.e. this supports a mapped system
resource return (e.g. a social share
deep link for a documentation resource)
which mapped resource itself is HTML
which also contains CRNRSTN :: mapped
system images.

This also creates a new layer of
application architecture within the
CLR-SSL supporting a TTL-able server-side
response cache buffer where pointers
to system file mapped resources (JS,
CSS, PNG,...) are cached in SESSION
during the HTML page build.

When the HTML page response gets to
the browser for rendering at the
client, and the mapped $_GET resource
requests start coming right back, the
server already has SESSION pointers
to the JS, CSS or PNG system file path
resources that were sent to the client
in the HTML <img>, <script>, 
<meta>,...etc. tags.

Therefore, we have the server in a
proper hands-off bind now where:

 1) building HTML automatically
    results in

 2) the server getting hot resource
    memory pointers that map straight
    to any image, JS, or CSS file
    whose URL happened to be built
    into the HTML page and sent
    to the client.

 3) When a browser loads HTML that
    has just been generated by
    the CLR-SSL, and the $_GET
    requests start coming back to
    the server, we have hot file
    pointers (TTL expire enabled)
    in SESSION memory for the
    immediate CRNRSTN :: PLAID
    buffer output return of the
    PNG, JPG, CSS, etc. data.

    The CRNRSTN :: RRS mapping
    architecture that is
    behind CRNRSTN :: PLAID is
    really fast!


5

